<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuva</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tannu Uriankhai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tuva is a republic of the Russian Federation in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, on the upper Yenisei, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. Inhabited mainly by Turkic-speaking Tuvans, it was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>'s Mongolian frontier until 1911, became a Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1914 and was the nominally independent Tuvan People's Republic from 1921. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> annexed it in 1944, and its people largely follow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhism</a> and shamanism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuva.jpg" alt="Tuva" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tuva.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
